<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Trenwick lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Trenwick lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said analyst Peter Wade downgraded property casualty reinsurance company Trenwick Group Inc to neutral from outperform.</p>
<p>-- said in summary report that downgrade was &quot;due to deteriorating market conditions which are significantly impacting the company's ability to grow.&quot;</p>
<p>-- cut 1997 earnings per share estimate to $3.05 from $3.20 and cut 1998 to $3.40 from $3.60.</p>
<p>-- has one-year price target of $43 on the stock.</p>
<p>-- shares were off 1-3/4 to 37-3/4.</p>
</text>
